WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.352
Start and controls
Take a seat and press Ready. The host starts when everyone is ready. Your cards or dice are at the bottom.

00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:19.653
Follow the turn prompt. Wait for animations to finish; an expired turn is played automatically. Use Return to room after settlement.

00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:35.652
Dou Dizhu: one against two
Three players use 54 cards: 17 each and 3 bottom cards. Follow Demo N through six deals using score bidding.

00:00:35.652 --> 00:00:48.852
Bid for landlord using score buttons
On your turn, press 1, 2, or 3, or pass. A bid must exceed the current score; a three confirms the landlord immediately.

00:00:48.852 --> 00:00:59.652
Bottom cards stay hidden during bidding. All passes redeal; repeated void auctions eventually force the opener to become landlord at one. Another room option uses call/grab bidding.

00:00:59.652 --> 00:01:09.552
Bottom cards appear after bidding
Demo E is now landlord. The three bottom cards are public and join that hand. The landlord leads; the other two players are allied farmers.

00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:17.652
The landlord has 20 cards and each farmer 17. The landlord wins by going out first; either farmer going out wins for both farmers.

00:01:17.652 --> 00:01:30.852
Select cards, then press Play
Click cards for a combination, check its type, and press Play. Clear resets the selection; Pass declines to follow.

00:01:30.852 --> 00:01:41.651
An ordinary response must have the same type and length and beat the current play. Two other passes give the last player a free lead, which cannot be passed.

00:01:41.651 --> 00:01:53.751
Farmer cooperation and combinations
Watch plays and passes. Farmers can save high cards and let their partner retain the lead.

00:01:53.751 --> 00:02:03.651
Singles, pairs, triples with attachments, straights, pair runs, airplanes, and four-with-two are supported. Runs exclude twos and jokers. Suits never break ties.

00:02:03.651 --> 00:02:16.851
Bombs and score multipliers
Speed through the rest of the first deal and watch its settlement once a player empties their hand.

00:02:16.851 --> 00:02:27.651
Four equal ranks alone form a bomb; both jokers form the strongest rocket. They beat ordinary combinations and double scores. Four-with-two is not a bomb; spring and anti-spring also double scores.

00:02:27.651 --> 00:02:36.451
One deal settles; another begins
The farmers won the first deal. Fresh cards are dealt and the opening bidder rotates. Each deal chooses a new landlord while totals carry forward.

00:02:36.451 --> 00:02:43.651
Deal scores use the base and multipliers. The landlord gains or loses twice each farmer’s amount; table scores sum to zero.

00:02:43.651 --> 00:03:27.652
Speed through five more deals
Every remaining auction, bottom-card reveal, play, and settlement runs in order at higher speed until deal six ends.

00:03:27.652 --> 00:03:46.667
Dou Dizhu: six-deal totals
Demo N wins with 7 points. Demo S has −2 and E has −5.
